<title>USA: FSA qualifies seven muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies seven muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Monday it qualified for bond insurance the following seven municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Glencoe, Minn., $1.8 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Sartell Independent School District No 748, Minn., $11.025 million GO refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Las Cruces School District No. 2, N.M., $10 million school building GOs.</p>
<p>--Lucas, Texas, $2.5 million certificates of obligation.</p>
<p>--Pearland Economic Development Authority, Texas, $5 million sales tax revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Menomonie, Wis., $2.655 million corporate purpose GOs.</p>
<p>--West Bend, Wis., $3.25 million GO promissory notes.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
